# Fast Build Configuration

If you follow the recommended approach and use a dedicated local repository for the integration tests (e.g. `target/local-repo`), you will likely encounter long build times. If the test repository has been cleaned, the plugin needs to re-download all artifacts from Maven Central and the resulting network traffic slows the test execution down.

But you can configure the plugin to download artifacts from your local repository instead.

To enable this feature, you have to add a `settings.xml` file in your project (for example in `src/it/settings.xml`) and modify the plugin configuration as this: 

```xml
<project>
  ...
  <build>
    <plugins>
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
        <artifactId>maven-invoker-plugin</artifactId>
        <version>${project.version}</version>
        <configuration>
          ...
          <settingsFile>src/it/settings.xml</settingsFile>
          ...
        </configuration>
      </plugin>
    </plugins>
  </build>
  ...
</project>
```

The settings must contain the following content which effectively tells Maven to use the local repository as a remote repository:

```xml
<?xml version="1.0"?>
<settings>
  <profiles>
    <profile>
      <id>it-repo</id>
      <repositories>
        <repository>
          <id>local.central</id>
          <url>@localRepositoryUrl@</url>
          <releases>
            <enabled>true</enabled>
          </releases>
          <snapshots>
            <enabled>true</enabled>
          </snapshots>
        </repository>
      </repositories>
      <pluginRepositories>
        <pluginRepository>
          <id>local.central</id>
          <url>@localRepositoryUrl@</url>
          <releases>
            <enabled>true</enabled>
          </releases>
          <snapshots>
            <enabled>true</enabled>
          </snapshots>
        </pluginRepository>
      </pluginRepositories>
    </profile>
  </profiles>
  <activeProfiles>
    <activeProfile>it-repo</activeProfile>
  </activeProfiles>
</settings>
```

The token `@localRepositoryUrl@` will be automatically replaced by the Invoker Plugin with the URL to the local repository used for the Maven invocation.

# Fast Build Configuration - mergeUserSettings and mirrors

If you use the Fast Build Configuration together with the `mergeUserSettings` parameter, check your mirror settings.

If you have in `~/.m2/settings.xml` something like:

```xml
<mirrors>
    <mirror>
        <id>mirrorId</id>
        <name>Public Mirrors</name>
        <url>url_to_my_mirror</url>
        <mirrorOf>*,!repo1,!repo2</mirrorOf>
    </mirror>
</mirrors>
```

Look at the `mirrorOf` element: a single `*` matches all repositories, including the repository with ID `local.central`, so the test builds download from the mirror and the Fast Build Configuration has no effect.

Change it to something like this:

```xml
<mirrors>
    <mirror>
        <id>mirrorId</id>
        <name>Public Mirrors</name>
        <url>url_to_my_mirror</url>
        <mirrorOf>external:*,!repo1,!repo2</mirrorOf>
    </mirror>
</mirrors>
```

`external:*` matches all repositories except those on `localhost` or with a `file:` URL.
